      "side": 1,
      "message": "ninja doesn\u0027t really care what the output is named, so dep_fixer just chose the last one, though I agree that\u0027s confusing in this case. It would be simple enough to take the first one, or the last non-empty one, or just a static value.\n\nIt seems rust emulated gcc/clang\u0027s -MP option, which isn\u0027t necessary with ninja (or dep_fixer)",
